@startuml membership-lifecycle
!include _theme.iuml

state "Not known to the organisation" as Unknown
state "Invited, waiting" as Invited
state "Invitation failed" as Failed
state "Member" as Member
state "Owner" as Owner
state "Outside collaborator" as Outside

[*] --> Unknown

Unknown --> Invited : members invite
note on link
  <b>Command, not declaration.</b> One login,
  confirmed, and the person is emailed.
end note

Invited --> Member : the person accepts
Invited --> Failed : GitHub records a reason
Invited --> Unknown : members remove
note on link
  The same endpoint withdraws an unanswered
  invitation and removes an active member.
end note

Member --> Owner : role changed in GitHub
Owner --> Member : role changed in GitHub

Member --> Outside : members convert
note on link
  Keeps only the repositories their current
  teams allow. Guarded exactly like a removal.
end note

Outside --> Unknown : members remove
Member --> Unknown : members remove
Owner --> Unknown : members remove

note right of Owner
  <b>Refused whatever else is true</b>
  • the only remaining owner
  • the account the run is authenticated as
end note

note bottom of Invited
  <b>inspect members</b> reports the age in whole
  days, which is what makes a stale invitation
  visible at all. A pending invitation counts as
  somebody already asked, so no run sends a
  second one.
end note
@enduml
